    "event": {
      "address": "Silk Street, London EC2Y 8DS",
      "category": "community",
      "dedupe_key": "black-british-book-festival-2026|2026-10-04|barbican",
      "description": "Back for its fifth year, the Black British Book Festival is a landmark celebration of Black books, ideas and culture with Candice Carty-Williams, Corinne Bailey Rae, Wretch 32 and more. Hear from Candice Carty-Williams on love, mess and the phenomenon of Queenie. Corinne Bailey Rae goes deep on sound, beauty and creative freedom. Wretch 32 makes the case that bars are literature, breaking down the art of the pen like never before. And closing it all out is The Black Poetry Shutdown with the UK's sharpest spoken-word talent such as Malika Booker, Lady Sanity, Jah Digga and more. Across the rest of the day, expect a line-up that spans literature, music, science, money, love, identity and the internet. There's something for everyone with storytelling, craft, superheroes and more for the youngest readers. Aspiring authors get a programme packed with practical, no-fluff sessions and the brand-new Black British Book Festival × Pan Macmillan collaboration - a real shot at getting published.",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.barbican.org.uk/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/images/2026-08/BBBF%20Main%20page%202026%20AUDIENCE%20Credit%20-%20Sledge%20Tshibangu.jpg.avif?itok=ihDA7J_e",
