      "date_text": "Sun 4 Oct 2026",
      "description": "\n  <p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Back for its fifth year, the Black British Book Festival is a landmark celebration of Black books, ideas and culture with <strong>Candice Carty-Williams, Corinne Bailey Rae, Wretch 32 </strong>and more.</span></p>\n\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hear from <strong>Candice Carty-Williams</strong> on love, mess and the phenomenon of </span><em><span lang=\"EN-US\">Queenie</span></em><span lang=\"EN-US\">. <strong>Corinne Bailey Rae </strong>goes deep on sound, beauty and creative freedom. <strong>Wretch 32 </strong>makes the case that bars are literature, breaking down the art of the pen like never before. And closing it all out is <strong>The Black Poetry Shutdown</strong> with the UK's sharpest spoken-word talent such as <strong>Malika Booker, Lady Sanity, Jah Digga</strong> and more.</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-US\">Across the rest of the day, expect a line-up that spans literature, music, science, money, love, identity and the internet.</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">There's something for everyone with storytelling, craft, superheroes and more for the youngest readers. Aspiring authors get a programme packed with practical, no-fluff sessions and the brand-new Black British Book Festival × Pan Macmillan collaboration - a real shot at getting published.</span></p>",
      "ends": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.barbican.org.uk/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/images/2026-08/BBBF%20Main%20page%202026%20AUDIENCE%20Credit%20-%20Sledge%20Tshibangu.jpg.avif?itok=ihDA7J_e",
